	<section class="bg-grey clear" id="types">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Types of payment options in online casinos</h2>
			<p>People are used to buying flight tickets, car accessories, pizza in a neighbouring cafe or app subscription, using credit and debit cards: Visa, Mastercard, AmEx, and local solutions of this kind. That is why novices usually think online casino payments are limited to the said options. But this is not how it works in online casinos.</p>
			<p>Trying to simplify the injection of funds into their platforms, online casinos are looking for ways to embrace as many payment instruments as possible. However, this is not always easy because of legal concerns, accessibility across countries, restrictions imposed by the payment provider, and many other factors. </p>
			<p>As a result, it is common practice that an average online casino has a smallish set of deposit and—even more so—withdrawal options. On the other hand, almost every online casino has a few (5 to 10 or even greater) cryptocurrencies to make up a shortfall in fiat options. Below, we delve into each type of payment system applied in online casino banking.</p>
		</div>
	</section>
