	<section id="cards">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Credit cards</h2>
			<p>The Discover card brand circulates mainly in the United States, while American Express has an international outreach, though it is not as popular as Visa and Mastercard, which are found in most online casinos worldwide. However, the ability to utilise your credit or debit card for gambling depends on a few factors, such as the country you are in, the online casino, and the card-issuing bank. Let’s review real-life cases that offer illuminating insights into cards in gambling:</p>
			<h3>Cases</h3>
			<ul class="cases">
				<li>An online casino accepts Visa. The country is friendly to online casino gambling. However, when the player got his Visa card in a bank establishment, he failed to choose an option that would have enabled him to make gambling-purpose transactions. So, when he tries to make an online casino deposit, the transaction does not go through.</li>
				<li>An online casino accepts Mastercard. The country is not friendly to online casino gambling, and neither is the player’s bank. However, the player’s dashboard in the casino shows Mastercard. He picks that option and gets redirected to the MC page, where he initiates and completes the payment successfully. How is that possible? It is an intentional miscoding of a transaction that hides its true nature (gambling)—some casinos recourse to this practice to bypass transaction deference.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>It is an empirical fact that global card options (Visa, MC, etc.) are offered in many offshore casinos that operate without local licenses or on territories where this kind of activity is forbidden (e.g. Australia). However, chances are low that online casino payments with credit cards will end in success in these environments.</p>
			<h3>Credit/debit cards: Pros & Cons</h3>
			<div class="pros-cons">
				<table class="pros">
					<tr>
						<th>
							<h4>Pros:</h4>
						</th>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Wide availability:</strong> Almost every offshore and licensed online casino has a credit card option for deposits and—more rarely—for withdrawals.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Low fees:</strong> Established by an issuing bank, these fees are in the 1% to 2% range.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>High safety:</strong> Banks take serious measures to protect transactions from hacking. Your funds are safe unless your device is infected with malware.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Universal solution:</strong> plastic cards are offered as two-way options in online casino banking: for deposits and cashouts.</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
				<table class="cons">
					<tr>
						<th>
							<h4>Cons:</h4>
						</th>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Denials:</strong> Some banks deny gambling transactions or suspend the funds for internal financial checks.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Taxation:</strong> Some countries, especially in Europe, make a person accountable for cash inflows to CCs, making it a lousy option for high rollers.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Currency conversion issues:</strong> If your bank account is in the local currency and the casino account is in the US $ or €, it cannot be ruled out that your bank has an unfavourable exchange rate, which can result in more funds being charged off.</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="bg-grey" id="e-wallets">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Electronic wallets</h2>
			<p>E-wallets act as intermediaries between a customer and a merchant. An electronic wallet keeps the person’s credit card numbers, personal information and other financial details required to make a transaction to/from online casinos or anywhere else. In some cases, an e-wallet holder must attach it to their bank account (Google Pay) because the software will not work without it.</p>
			<p>Other digital wallets (Skrill, Neteller) give users the flexibility to pay with their uploaded funds or debit (credit) cards, so you have a choice of pre-funding your account and using the money later; or paying for your items directly with any of the credit cards attached to your e-wallet account. It's always a good idea to have a mix of payment methods with you, and electronic wallets are a great way of handling money without the inconvenience of being rejected by the bank. </p>
			<p>In many situations, electronic wallets are preferable to credit cards because the former offers flexibility and extra features unavailable in credit cards. Digital wallets allow one to make international payments from countries where credit card issuers deny gambling transactions. </p>
			<p>E-wallets are ideal in locations with a low level of international credit card usage. For example, in Kenya, they have a local payment solution, M-Pesa, that has almost overtaken MC and Visa in online casinos banking. </p>
			<h3>Tip</h3>
			<p class="tip">If the online casino accepts cards and e-wallets, and you have both, make the former your first choice, especially with a significant volume of deposits. The reason is simple: most digital wallets apply fees which are typically higher than those of bank cards.</p>
			<h3>Cases</h3>
			<ul class="cases">
				<li>A player from South Africa wants to make a $100 Skrill deposit (in ZAR equivalent) to an online casino. Everything goes smoothly, but the total amount charged is $102.5 because of a 2.5% fee. If the player had transferred $100 through Visa, he would have paid $101 (a standard 1% applies). Inference: e-wallets are not the cheapest option.</li>
				<li>A player wants to claim a first-deposit bonus. He signs up with a casino and uses Neteller to transfer some money to the casino balance. Surprisingly, the site denies claiming the bonus. The player opens the general bonus t&c and reads that Neteller does not qualify for the bonus program. Explanation: online casinos typically absorb deposit fees because they are petty, but with some e-wallets, casinos can ill afford to absorb them.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>Many online casino players favour e-wallets due to the many benefits they carry. We are not going to discuss security here because every serious e-wallet provider makes its product extremely secure. On the other hand, every payment option can be compromised, much because of user negligence or mistakes—just remember that hackers can figure out how to get through even the safest options. Below are the features that online casino players love in many digital wallets.</p>
			<h3>Electronic wallets: Pros & Cons</h3>
			<div class="pros-cons">
				<table class="pros">
					<tr>
						<th>
							<h4>Pros:</h4>
						</th>
					</tr>
