	<section id="vouchers">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Prepaid vouchers</h2>
			<p>This option is helpful if you have issues with a credit card or don’t want to deal with e-wallets. Vouchers are present in many online casinos, but there are few driving forces to use them unless you live in a place where all other financial solutions are not accessible for some reason or other.</p>
			<p>A voucher (Neosurf, paysafecard, Astropay) represents a unique code (typically 16 digits). A user buys it online or at a sales outlet as a receipt and then types the digits on the online casino banking page. </p>
			<p>Vouchers come in fixed denominations that usually match their actual price. For example, the paysafecard has four face values: $10, $25, $50, and $100 (or equivalent sums in other currencies in 50+ countries where it is distributed). Its cost can be a bit higher if you buy it from resellers, who add a small surcharge.</p>
			<p>Let’s expound on the scenarios where prepaid cards can be of help in online casinos banking:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>The online casino offers few payment options in your country, so you might want to buy a voucher for want of a better.</li>
				<li>All minimum deposit limits, except for electronic vouchers, are higher than normal for you in your preferred casino.</li>
				<li>You have a compulsive personality, so you want to limit your casino expenses to some fixed amount. That’s why you buy an eVoucher that will naturally prevent you from laying out more money than the voucher’s value.</li>
			</ul>
			<h3>Tips</h3>
			<ul class="cases">
				<li>It is not mandatory that you zero out your voucher, putting all the money into the casino account at once. If you bought a $50 code but want to deposit half, you can do this easily. To that end, you must create an account (myPaysafe, myNeosurf) on the payment platform’s website. After that, you may split a voucher, with your unused part being stored in your account for future payments. In a similar way, you may combine voucher PINs into one so the balance can be used for a bigger deposit to an online casino.</li>
				<li>However counter-intuitive it may seem, some vouchers can be used as a withdrawal option in online casinos. If you have a myNeosurf account and deposited to the casino with a Neosurf PIN, you can cash out the winnings back if the casino allows this option.</li>
				<li>Mind that most brands set an expiration date on the vouchers. Users have a few years (terms vary) to use it until it becomes invalid. Some vouchers deduct a service fee from the remaining balance after a certain period of inactivity (e.g. $2 after 24 months in paysafecard)</li>
			</ul>
			<h3>Prepaid vouchers: Pros & Cons</h3>
			<div class="pros-cons">
				<table class="pros">
					<tr>
						<th>
							<h4>Pros:</h4>
						</th>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Budget under control:</strong> Due to the nature of a voucher, you will not spend more than its value.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>No deposit fee:</strong> Deposits to online casinos with prepaid codes are usually free of commissions.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Easy to get:</strong> Players face no problems trying to find and acquire a PIN.</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
				<table class="cons">
					<tr>
						<th>
							<h4>Cons:</h4>
						</th>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Withdrawal problems:</strong> Many voucher brands support incoming transactions, but online casinos rarely offer this, forcing users to fall back on alternative options.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Risk of loss:</strong> A receipt with the printed PIN can get lost if treated improperly. PINs are non-recoverable.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><strong>Bonus issues:</strong> Excluded from bonuses in some casinos (This especially applies to paysafecard).</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</div>

		</div>
	</section>

	<section id="crypto" class="bg-grey">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Cryptocurrency</h2>
			<p>Around three-fourths of online casinos accept cryptocurrency for deposit and pay out winnings in digital coins. Moreover, many casinos allow betting in crypto. Setting up a crypto wallet and buying tokens is not a challenging task because many online casinos have explicit instructions on where to buy, how to store, and how to transfer crypto. There are over a hundred varieties of cryptocurrencies (Bitcoin, Ethereum, Tether, Dogecoin, and so on), and a typical casino features over ten of them on the banking page.</p>
			<p>Most gambling and betting sites combine fiat and crypto for players’ convenience. Still, there are many crypto-only brands where cryptocurrencies are the only options for deposit and cashout. Currently, this is one of the best online casino banking options because of its numerous advantages. Sure, a player will have to find a reliable exchange and buy the crypto first, but it’s as easy as shooting fish in a barrel. </p>
			<p>Some online casinos have bonuses given away on crypto deposits, which is another incentive for some players to use digital assets. Online casino brands generally have few bonuses that are beneficial for players, given unrealistic wagering requirements, but those granted on crypto deposits are friendlier in many respects.</p>
			<h3>Tips</h3>
			<ul class="cases">
				<li>Choose a crypto if you are going to deposit petty cash. A normal minimum deposit is $10 for fiat options and half as much for crypto. Consult your cashier page for exact limits. </li>
				<li>If you have fiat and crypto and the online casino accepts both, take time to discern for yourselves the one that suits you best. Look at bonus terms and banking limits. Mind that crypto bets are not accepted in some games.</li>
			</ul>
			<h3>Cryptocurrency: Pros & Cons</h3>
			<div class="pros-cons">
				<table class="pros">
					<tr>
						<th>
							<h4>Pros:</h4>
						</th>
					</tr>
					<tr>
